clauses.plain_english:
The receiving side must:
- use information only for the Purpose;
- share it only with need-to-know employees, directors, advisers and subcontractors who are bound in writing;
- take reasonable care;
- promptly report any leak.

clauses.reason:
Clause 2.1 lists 'sales and customer data', so LoopMart may share shopper personal data during pre-sales discussions. This is a human judgement call, not a defect in the wording. Before signing, you may want to confirm:
- whether personal data will actually be shared at NDA stage;
- whether de-identified or sample data would be enough;
- that AtliQ can meet DPDP obligations for it.

The clause sets no breach-notice timeframe, which is lighter than past commitments (Meridian 24h, R-051; Trustline 6h, R-055). The data type is 'other personal data', not health or payment data, so it was not treated as a regulated-data escalation trigger. A human should confirm that judgement.
